{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits","id":929686,"title":"Hunter 2e: Hunters and Supernatural Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T06:32:34-07:00","id":929686,"title":"Hunter 2e: Hunters and Supernatural Merits","content":"One of the things I'll be most interested in with Hunter 2e (and I'll be super disappointed if there isn't at least a sidebar addressing this) is how the game will handle the new supernatural merits that have been introduced in the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook and Hurt Locker?<br /> <br /> How will they interact with Endowments? Will Endowments be made into Supernatural Merits for simplicity's sake?<br /> <br /> But all of that is stuff we don't know yet. What we can talk about is how we personally would handle them. In what situations would it be a good idea to let Hunter characters take Supernatural Merits? And how do you think this would work from an in-universe perspective? Someone who can light things on fire with his mind is going to have a somewhat rocky relationship with the Hunter community. He might feel more kinship with the monsters, based on what course his life has taken. Regardless of how human he is, other hunters might consider him dangerously close to being a monster. Cheiron might want to carve him up and study him. TFV might want him chipped and monitored. <br /> <br /> That opens the door to discussing how &quot;human+&quot; characters (as opposed to characters enhanced beyond human by enhancements) operate within the various Compacts and Conspiracies. Obviously, some of them try to keep it hidden, which has plenty of plot potential. Since VASCU is made up of &quot;natural psychics&quot;, I could see them being an advocate in the larger Hunter community, using themselves as an example of how not every esper is a Carrie waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:02:01-07:00","id":929698,"title":"","content":"According to a question I once asked David in the Hurt Locker thread, Endowments (or at least, some of them) are considered Supernatural Merits in relation to the Supernatural Tolerance merit, and I think that they always were (at least, conceptually). They are simply a form of Supernatural Merits which are easy to acquire for any member of a Conspiracy. Witchfinder did in fact discussed the matter a bit, I think (under Gifted Hunters). All in all, the major difference between Endowments and regular Supernatural Merits is that the later simply &quot;happen&quot; to the character. When enough people acquire more or less the same merit, through more or less the same method, and it can be recreated and used to give it to new members, the merit turns into a true Endowment.<br /> <br /> On the other note, maybe it's just me, but I can't say there is anything &quot;natural&quot; in the Wintergreen Process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:54:39-07:00","id":929764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=929698#post929698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to a question I once asked David in the Hurt Locker thread, Endowments (or at least, some of them) are considered Supernatural Merits in relation to the Supernatural Tolerance merit, and I think that they always were (at least, conceptually). They are simply a form of Supernatural Merits which are easy to acquire for any member of a Conspiracy. Witchfinder did in fact discussed the matter a bit, I think (under Gifted Hunters). All in all, the major difference between Endowments and regular Supernatural Merits is that the later simply &quot;happen&quot; to the character. When enough people acquire more or less the same merit, through more or less the same method, and it can be recreated and used to give it to new members, the merit turns into a true Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>So, basicly, all Conspiracy level hunters are Sleepwalkers?!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Gosh, I did not see this coming! And I like implications of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum, Knights of St. Gorge and Order of Nameless - preper to kick my players mages asses! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:10:12-07:00","id":929778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=929764#post929764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>So, basicly, all Conspiracy level hunters are Sleepwalkers?!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Gosh, I did not see this coming! And I like implications of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum, Knights of St. Gorge and Order of Nameless - preper to kick my players mages asses! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see advanced armory as being specially supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:48:52-07:00","id":929825,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it depends on the endowment. Elixir for example would only make you a sleepwalker whilst actually under the effects of it, relic would probably only for the time that you're actively using a relic. If it grants an innate power it'll turn you into a sleepwalker, if it temporarily grants one then it will make you one when the power is granted to you and if it is an item it depends on the items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T10:56:05-07:00","id":929832,"title":"","content":"I imagine some Endowments will be Mental, some Physical, some Social, and some Supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:03:07-07:00","id":929953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=929825#post929825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it depends on the endowment. Elixir for example would only make you a sleepwalker whilst actually under the effects of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elixir is a supernatural ability to turn poisons you drink into harmless substances. There's nothing normal about being able to drink mercury then turn it to water inside your stomach.<br /> <br /> (I hope that 2E lets Elixir defend you against being poisoned and similar, I don't think it would be a particularly useful ability, but the fluff says you should be able to do it)<br /> <br /> <br /> The only Conspiracy tier Endowments that I would say are non-Supernatural is Advanced Armoury and Relic. And I'd expect that the AKD will get a Supernatural benefit from Status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:39:48-07:00","id":929971,"title":"","content":"Eh, easy enough to handwave Advanced Armory privilege only granted by TFV after you go through a two-week long Mental Defense Training course, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:15:32-07:00","id":930018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=929764#post929764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malleus Maleficarum, Knights of St. Gorge and Order of Nameless - preper to kick my players mages asses! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't your players one-hit Hastur? You might need more than a few sleepwalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T22:50:17-07:00","id":930182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=929832#post929832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine some Endowments will be Mental, some Physical, some Social, and some Supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>...huh. Breaking Endowments down into categories the way regular Merits are actually makes a lot of sense, and answers the question of how to give mechanical support to non-supernatural groups like most Compacts.<br /> <br /> I really like this idea, especially if there are generic Endowments for all groups and/or homebrew setups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T00:49:34-07:00","id":930230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=930018#post930018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't your players one-hit Hastur? You might need more than a few sleepwalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>King in Yellow</i> is one Royal Avatar - Conspiracies have hundreds, or even thousands of agents worldwide... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T21:25:30-07:00","id":930706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=930182#post930182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...huh. Breaking Endowments down into categories the way regular Merits are actually makes a lot of sense, and answers the question of how to give mechanical support to non-supernatural groups like most Compacts.<br /> <br /> I really like this idea, especially if there are generic Endowments for all groups and/or homebrew setups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I wouldn't mind that at all. But then, I've always been a fan of the notion that there needs to be at least a partial decoupling of Endowments from Tier 3; so I love the idea of redefining \u201cEndowment\u201d as \u201ca Merit that is usually provided by a hunter org\u201d, with a note that most (but not all) Supernatural Endowments are provided by Conspiracies, and that most (but not all) Conspiracies provide Supernatural Endowments. TFV and AKD serve as examples of Conspiracies that arguably don't provide Supernatural Endowments (if one defines \u201cSupernatural Merit\u201d as \u201ca Merit that makes you supernatural\u201d \u2014 or, in <b>Mage</b> parlance, a Merit that makes you a Sleepwalker); and if the Cainite Heresy and Les Mysteres can be reclassified as Compacts due to their lack of organizational structure, they'd serve nicely as Compacts that grant Supernatural Endowments. <br /> <br /> Then bring in the Compact Endowments from <b>Compacts and Conspiracies</b> as examples of Physical, Mental, and Social Endowments. <br /> <br /> I'd even allow independent Cells to devise their own Endowments \u2014 but with the caveat that doing so generally requires a chronicle's worth of effort. Endowments are generally not something that your average mortal can cook up in his basement or find lying around, the most notable exceptions being Relics (AKD has a huge supply of Relics; but they don't hold a monopoly on them) and Prayer (a member of the Long Night, likewise, is merely <i>more likely</i> than your typical religiously devout individual to truly believe in the power of prayer, and that's merely because he's more likely to have his faith tested on a regular basis: that which doesn't break you makes you stronger). That all goes doubly so for <i>Supernatural</i> Endowments. <br /> <br /> So <i>in principle</i>, anyone could have an Endowment, of any type; but <i>in practice</i>, you'll rarely find Physical, Mental,or Social Endowments outside the Compacts, and you'll rarely find Supernatural Endowments outside the Conspiracies. <br /> <br /> <br /> Note also that Thaumaturge Merits could be thought of as Supernatural \u201cEndowments\u201d provided by \u201cCompacts\u201d (i.e., the various Thaumaturge Traditions, which are arguably as organized as the Cainite Heresy). And if it were me, I'd draw parallels between Malleus Maleficatorum (whose Benedictions are not unlike Theban Sorcery, in concept if not implementation) and the Sons of Phobos. <br /> <br /> Heck, I'd love to get a \u201cCancer Cells\u201d supplement that focuses on <b>Hunter</b> as a <i>true</i> crossover game, with a dual focus on how hunters would interact with the <i>actual</i> powers of the other gamelines, and on hunter cells that, for various reasons, choose to work <i>with</i> the Shadow Folk instead of working against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:04:08-07:00","id":930968,"title":"","content":"You know what would be cool? If Endowments weren't even restricted to Hunters!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> No, wait, hear me out.<br /> <br /> Basically, Endowments would be Merits of the appropriate type with <i>hefty</i> drawbacks. Like using Elixir would poison a normal person, Castigations would ravage your soul, all that good stuff. What Compacts/Conspiracies do is make the Endowments <i>safer</i>, as well as making it easier/more convenient for you to pick up new powers.<br /> <br /> Add onto that the idea that some Conspiracies see certain Endowments as their <i>property</i>. If you use Castigations, you're gonna be visited by members of the Lucifuge who want you to join (or else). And if you <i>do</i> join, you might actually get a power <i>boost</i> for some of your Castigations, since you're actually using them <i>correctly</i> now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:41:18-07:00","id":935717,"title":"","content":"That does kind of make some sense. If you wanted to decouple Castigations from demonic heritage, you could always say that it was possible to use them (with major drawbacks) by making deals with demons (which would be helpful to Hunter players who want to make demonologist characters without having to buy Inferno).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:48:12-07:00","id":936066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=935717#post935717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(which would be helpful to Hunter players who want to make demonologist characters without having to buy Inferno).</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you just use the ephemeral rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T11:53:30-07:00","id":936178,"title":"","content":"Well, I meant specifically representing a character using Castigations. I like the idea that they work by contract, and someone without infernal ancestry would only be able to &quot;borrow&quot; them, meaning that the merit would give them a set amount of times they could use a Castigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:33:41-07:00","id":936245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=936178#post936178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I meant specifically representing a character using Castigations. I like the idea that they work by contract, and someone without infernal ancestry would only be able to &quot;borrow&quot; them, meaning that the merit would give them a set amount of times they could use a Castigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/845732-pacts-for-everyone\">this</a> thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:16:32-07:00","id":936267,"title":"","content":"I have not, that's interesting. Though I'll reiterate that I was talking specifically about amechra's idea of making Endowments not exclusive to Conspiracies but having risks for using them independently, we just got a bit off topic. <br /> <br /> Advanced Armory is one that's probably the most discussed in terms of people not in TFV using it. I'd say there that the &quot;cost&quot; for unauthorized use is the difficulty of obtaining it and removing the locks and the risk of TFV finds out you have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:34:34-07:00","id":936274,"title":"","content":"A lot of Advanced Armory would probably also degrade without regular maintenance, requiring either materials or technical knowledge that non-TFV members generally won't have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:12:40-07:00","id":936362,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, that's definitely another one to take note of. One of the reasons why the technology used in AA isn't in wide usage is because they haven't figured out how to make it durable/user friendly/cheap, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:42:07-07:00","id":963304,"title":"","content":"&quot;Heck, I'd love to get a \u201cCancer Cells\u201d supplement that focuses on Hunter as a true crossover game, with a dual focus on how hunters would interact with the actual powers of the other gamelines, and on hunter cells that, for various reasons, choose to work with the Shadow Folk instead of working against them.&quot;<br /> <br /> You mean a book like a crossover chronicle ;p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:28:13-07:00","id":963419,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it seems worth a Compact; people with one foot in the shadow no matter how hard they try, and who band together against those who see them as interlopers or prestigious slaves. At the least, I know I'm gonna try to work something out once Hunter 2e comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:49:31-07:00","id":963892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=936267#post936267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not, that's interesting. Though I'll reiterate that I was talking specifically about amechra's idea of making Endowments not exclusive to Conspiracies but having risks for using them independently, we just got a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> Advanced Armory is one that's probably the most discussed in terms of people not in TFV using it. I'd say there that the &quot;cost&quot; for unauthorized use is the difficulty of obtaining it and removing the locks and the risk of TFV finds out you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Castigations thing, note that Inferno speaks of enfants terrible (IIRC) who are basically potential Lucifuge who have escaped the notice of that Conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:04:52-07:00","id":965279,"title":"","content":"Something to remember is that Advanced Armory won't work for anyone who doesn't have a TFV microchip implant. How hard that lock is to break isn't really discussed, but in my own canon it isn't entirely mundane. The chip acts like a brand identifying members of a mystery cult and allowing them access to its &quot;magic.&quot; Heck, given that the Mortal Remains rules for Demon suggest simulating them with Advanced Armory one could make the argument that Advanced Armory is just a techgnostic version of Relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:08:53-07:00","id":965283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=965279#post965279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to remember is that Advanced Armory won't work for anyone who doesn't have a TFV microchip implant. How hard that lock is to break isn't really discussed, but in my own canon it isn't entirely mundane. The chip acts like a brand identifying members of a mystery cult and allowing them access to its &amp;quot;magic.&amp;quot; Heck, given that the Mortal Remains rules for Demon suggest simulating them with Advanced Armory one could make the argument that Advanced Armory is just a techgnostic version of Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd bet good money that RFID chip has some kind of Norse runes on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:13:40-07:00","id":965293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=965283#post965283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd bet good money that RFID chip has some kind of Norse runes on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense, that's just the way the circuits are laid out. A trick of the light and a superstitious mind. Don't be ridiculous, man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:48:13-07:00","id":968416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=965283#post965283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd bet good money that RFID chip has some kind of Norse runes on it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Psst, no one is supposed to know that's the language of the Roswell survivors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:52:34-07:00","id":968652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=968416#post968416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Psst, no one is supposed to know that's the language of the Roswell survivors!</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own mind TFV's supernaturally-inflected tech and Norse fetishism came from cross-pollination with things they brought back from Europe after WWII. Something the Loyalists of Thule definitely don't know anything about and you shouldn't ask them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:02:19-07:00","id":972874,"title":"","content":"I think both the idea of turning endowments into merits and the idea of making endowments potentially available to everyone are great ideas that really play to the strengths of the game.<br /> <br /> What I love about Hunter is that it's basically a modular game that covers a whole range of styles and moods. You can either take the setting whole cloth or you can detach the components to tell very specific and focused types of stories. I think detaching the endowments from specific conspiracies (but having each one as the canon specialization for a conspiracy/compact) would nicely parallel the sort of grab bag nature of dread powers.<br /> <br /> I doubt it would fit in the core, but I'd love to see a book that really digs into the bone and gristle of endowments and dread powers. Say the first half of the book covers endowments. Each section focuses on the drawbacks to each and outlines how these powers could work in various tiered games. Introduce drawbacks that become increasingly more severe if you're buying them as someone not of the preferred compact/conspiracy, and escalating as you're lower on the tier totem pole. Then focus on some general guidelines for creating new endowments in each category. Treat the second half of the book as a compendium of dread powers, categorized according to what type of supernatural is most inclined to have them. I'd buy that book first day, and it would get a whole lot of use from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:58:00-07:00","id":972919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=972874#post972874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think both the idea of turning endowments into merits and the idea of making endowments potentially available to everyone are great ideas that really play to the strengths of the game.<br /> <br /> What I love about Hunter is that it's basically a modular game that covers a whole range of styles and moods. You can either take the setting whole cloth or you can detach the components to tell very specific and focused types of stories. I think detaching the endowments from specific conspiracies (but having each one as the canon specialization for a conspiracy/compact) would nicely parallel the sort of grab bag nature of dread powers.<br /> <br /> I doubt it would fit in the core, but I'd love to see a book that really digs into the bone and gristle of endowments and dread powers. Say the first half of the book covers endowments. Each section focuses on the drawbacks to each and outlines how these powers could work in various tiered games. Introduce drawbacks that become increasingly more severe if you're buying them as someone not of the preferred compact/conspiracy, and escalating as you're lower on the tier totem pole. Then focus on some general guidelines for creating new endowments in each category. Treat the second half of the book as a compendium of dread powers, categorized according to what type of supernatural is most inclined to have them. I'd buy that book first day, and it would get a whole lot of use from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly what I want. Custom monsters, and easy to assemble hunter conspiracies. Have they given any indication they intend to do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:35:19-07:00","id":972933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=972874#post972874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think both the idea of turning endowments into merits and the idea of making endowments potentially available to everyone are great ideas that really play to the strengths of the game.<br /> <br /> What I love about Hunter is that it's basically a modular game that covers a whole range of styles and moods. You can either take the setting whole cloth or you can detach the components to tell very specific and focused types of stories. I think detaching the endowments from specific conspiracies (but having each one as the canon specialization for a conspiracy/compact) would nicely parallel the sort of grab bag nature of dread powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I experimented a while back with a system for doing pretty much exactly that. I gave it up though because the more I got into it the more it seemed to be stripping out a lot of the individual flavor from each Conspiracy and Endowment. <br /> <br /> That being said I think a single stream-lined system for purchasing Endowments (rather than each one having its own slightly different system) would be a big boon, as well as make it easier to just re-skin an Endowment for another Conspiracy if you wanted to. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:22:28-07:00","id":972958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=972919#post972919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty much exactly what I want. Custom monsters, and easy to assemble hunter conspiracies. Have they given any indication they intend to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure. I was following open dev pretty closely right when the game was announced, but I haven't really checked in on the updates in months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:26:55-07:00","id":972963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/929686-hunter-2e-hunters-and-supernatural-merits?p=972933#post972933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I experimented a while back with a system for doing pretty much exactly that. I gave it up though because the more I got into it the more it seemed to be stripping out a lot of the individual flavor from each Conspiracy and Endowment.<br /> <br /> That being said I think a single stream-lined system for purchasing Endowments (rather than each one having its own slightly different system) would be a big boon, as well as make it easier to just re-skin an Endowment for another Conspiracy if you wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah. Don't get me wrong. I love that each compact and conspiracy has their own flavor, and I'd make it so the canon setting essentially has each endowment tied to a specific compact/conspiracy; but I'm all about rules that make modular conversion easier, especially if it's partnered with potential mechanical disadvantages and setting flavor.<br /> <br /> If I were to homebrew a system, I'd probably partner each endowment with suggested recurring or persistent conditions. Continued use of castigation could force integrity checks. Thamatech might trigger nausea or specific derangements depending on the type of tech. Elixirs come with increasingly more severe addictions. etc. etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-20-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://foru